BB_NO_NETWORK = '0'
_EOF
	(build-host)$ export PATH=$PATH:<PROJECT_DIR>/layers/meta-xilinx/gen-machine-conf/

7.2.2.3 Choose design
---------------------
a. For Flat Design:
	(build-host)$ gen-machineconf parse-sdt --hw-description <path_to_dir/my-project-dir> -c conf/ --machine-name <your_workflow_machine_name> --add-config CONFIG_SUBSYSTEM_MACHINE_NAME=\"zynqmp-zcu102-rev1.1\"
b. For Full Design:
	(build-host)$ gen-machineconf parse-sdt --hw-description <path_to_dir/my-project-dir> -c conf/ --machine-name <your_workflow_machine_name> --add-config CONFIG_SUBSYSTEM_MACHINE_NAME=\"zynqmp-zcu102-rev1.1\" -g full

7.2.2.4 Build image
-------------------
	(build-host)$ cat << _EOF >> conf/local.conf
WORKFLOW_MACHINE_NAME = "<your_workflow_machine_name>"
_EOF
	(build-host)$ bitbake wrlinux-image-std

NOTE:
1. The name for "<your_workflow_machine_name>" must NOT be the following names:
	- zynqmp-zcu102-sdt-full
Because this name has been occupied by the configuration file in the layer
meta-amd-adaptive-socs-bsp. "wrlinux-zynqmp-zcu102-sdt" is a usable name.

2. If you need to re-run gen-machineconf under an old project, you must clear
the project first:
	(build-host)$ rm conf/machine -Rf; rm output -Rf; rm conf/dts -Rf; rm hw-description -Rf
	(build-host)$ sed -i '/WORKFLOW_MACHINE_NAME/d' conf/local.conf
And after re-running the gen-machineconf command, do not forget to add
WORKFLOW_MACHINE_NAME back to conf/local.conf according to the type of
XSA file.

7.3 Device Tree Overlay
-----------------------
The Device Tree Overlay(DTO) is used to add the child nodes and the fragments
from the .dtbo file to the base device tree, then triggering drivers to be
probed after PL programming. So the dtbo file for PL needs to be installed
to rootfs along with .bit files.

7.3.1 SDT Configuration
-----------------------
The recipe "zynqmp-fw-demo" in the amd-zynqmp bsp layer is used to install
dtbo file to WRLinux by utilizing the bbclass "dfx_user_dts". For a more
detailed description of "dfx_user_dts", please see
	https://github.com/Xilinx/meta-xilinx/blob/rel-v2025.2/docs/README.dfx.user.dts.md

After running the steps in "7.2.2 SDT Workflow", execute the following commands:

	(build-host)$ cd <PROJECT_DIR>; . ./environment-setup-x86_64-wrlinuxsdk-linux; . ./oe-init-build-env
	(build-host)$ cp conf/dts/<your_workflow_machine_name>/pl-overlay-full/pl.dtsi <PROJECT_DIR>/layers/amd-zynqmp/recipes-firmware/zynqmp-fw-demo/files
	(build-host)$ cp hw-description/<path_to_bit>/<proj>.bit <PROJECT_DIR>/layers/amd-zynqmp/recipes-firmware/zynqmp-fw-demo/files
	(build-host)$ cat << _EOF >> conf/local.conf
IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " zynqmp-fw-demo"
CUSTOMER_RECIPES:wr-amd-zynqmp += 'zynqmp-fw-demo'
FW_DEMO_FILES:pn-zynqmp-fw-demo = "pl.dtsi <proj>.bit"
_EOF
	(build-host)$ bitbake wrlinux-image-std

The dtbo and pdi files can be found at the boards:
	root@amd-zynqmp:~# ls -l /lib/firmware/xilinx/zynqmp-fw-demo/zynqmp-fw-demo.*
	-rw-r--r-- 1 root root    3825 Apr  5  2011 /lib/firmware/xilinx/zynqmp-fw-demo/zynqmp-fw-demo.dtbo
	-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 1423280 Apr  5  2011 /lib/firmware/xilinx/zynqmp-fw-demo/zynqmp-fw-demo.bin

And these two files can be used to program PL by following the instructions
in "7.4 PL Programming".

7.4 PL Programming
------------------
There are 3 methods to program PL from the Linux side:
    - sysfs
    - configfs
    - fpgautil

For a more detailed description of PL programming, please see
	https://xilinx-wiki.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/A/pages/18841847/Solution+ZynqMP+PL+Programming

7.4.1 Sysfs
-----------
Run the following commands to program PL with the bitstream file via sysfs:

	root@amd-zynqmp:~# echo 0 > /sys/class/fpga_manager/fpga0/flags
	root@amd-zynqmp:~# mkdir -p /lib/firmware
	root@amd-zynqmp:~# cp <path_to_bin/proj.bin> /lib/firmware/
	root@amd-zynqmp:~# echo proj.bin > /sys/class/fpga_manager/fpga0/firmware

7.4.2 Configfs
--------------
Run the following commands to program PL with the PDI file via configfs:

	root@amd-zynqmp:~# echo 0 > /sys/class/fpga_manager/fpga0/flags
	root@amd-zynqmp:~# mkdir -p /lib/firmware
	root@amd-zynqmp:~# cp <path_to_bin/proj.bin> /lib/firmware/
	root@amd-zynqmp:~# cp <path_to_dtbo/pl.dtbo> /lib/firmware/
	root@amd-zynqmp:~# mkdir /sys/kernel/config/device-tree/overlays/system
	root@amd-zynqmp:~# cd /lib/firmware/
	root@amd-zynqmp:~# echo pl.dtbo > /sys/kernel/config/device-tree/overlays/system/path

Steps to remove the drivers got added as part of DTO

	root@amd-zynqmp:~# rmdir /sys/kernel/config/device-tree/overlays/system

7.4.3 Fpgautil
--------------
The fpgautil tool provides a user-friendly interface for loading,
reconfiguring and reading FPGA bitstream configurations. Follow
the steps to install this tool on WRLinux:

	(build-host)$ cd <PROJECT_DIR>; . ./environment-setup-x86_64-wrlinuxsdk-linux; . ./oe-init-build-env
	(build-host)$ cat << _EOF >> conf/local.conf
CUSTOMER_RECIPES:xilinx += 'fpga-manager-script'
IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " fpga-manager-script"
_EOF

Run the following commands to program PL with the PDI file via fpgautil:
    root@amd-zynqmp:~# fpgautil -b <path_to_bin/proj.bin> -o <path_to_dtbo/pl.dtbo>
